  "answer": "The Manual lists the following suggested alternatives to ‘monitoring services’. These are examination practice, not legislative wording requirements. [TMM/Part14/x-14.-annex-a13-list-of-terms-too-broad-for-classification/monitoring-services]\n\n| Suggested alternative | Class |\n|---|---|\n| Market demand monitoring services | 35 |\n| Monitoring of investment portfolios | 36 |\n| Monitoring of package shipments | 39 |\n| Monitoring of computer system operation by remote access | 42 |\n| Monitoring of patients | 44 |\n| Monitoring of alarms | 45 |\n| Monitoring intellectual property rights for legal advisory purposes | 45 |\n\nAll entries above are supported by the Manual’s ‘monitoring-services’ passage cited above.\n\nSeparately, the Regulations require goods and services to be grouped according to their appropriate classes and the applicant to nominate the appropriate class number for each group. [TMR1995/r4.4]"
